{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/reviews/id38161240"}, "name":{"label":"patchesrefit"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-11-01T12:35:42-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"2025.11"}, "id":{"label":"13343667469"}, "title":{"label":"I Love Overcast"}, "content":{"label":"It’s been several years now I’ve been using this player, and I’ve got more than enough listening, to serve me for years to come.. mostly because of the brilliant folks who share on Reddit subs (r/podcasts), but I’m here to review Overcast.. yeah, it might not be for everyone because it doesn’t look like Netflix, it doesn’t hunt around looking for ideas for you, but there are other ways of looking for new podcasts.. what Overcast does best is play and manage my podcasts.. I’m able to find, follow, store, sort, create playlists, toggle features to download, display, and delete automatically, buzz me if something new comes in on favourites, and it’s on all of the usual feeds and distribution lists.. so there’s no hiccups there.. what I first loved about Overcast, and it has never let me down, is how I am able to adjust the speed and voice spacing between sentences — which is something so difficult to do and Overcast nails it out of all the players out there — making this simple, reliable, very affordable, and technically advanced player my choice for best in class. Love. ♥️", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/ca/review?id=888422857&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
